<section id="karolijn">
<h1 class="persona_title">Caroline suffers from RSI</h1>
<img src={Karolijn.src} class="stretch" alt="Caroline" />
</section>

<section>
	<blockquote>
<p>"I have a lot of pain in my wrist and shoulder due to Repetitive Strain Injury. Thanks to speech recognition software, I can give my arm some much-needed rest."</p>
</blockquote>
</section>

<section>
<h2>Examples</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a target="tweede" href="https://www.youtube.com/embed/kJKQmTumFP0?autoplay=1&amp;start=46">Dragon Naturally Speaking</a> (Windows)</li>
    <li><a target="tweede" href="https://support.apple.com/en-us/HT210539">Voice Control</a> (macOS, Catalina)</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section>
<p>Caroline cannot activate an icon when its name is not clear.</p>
</section>

<section>
<img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/icones/twitter_iconen.png" alt="twitter interface with several icons without text (for example a hash tag symbol)"/>

</section>

<section>
<img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/icones/twitter_iconen_met_tekst.jpg" alt="twitter interface where icons have visible labels (for example 'explore' for the hashtag)" />

</section>

<section>
<h2>Best practice</h2>
<ul>
<li>Give icons a visible label</li>
<li>Use meaningful links and alternative texts</li>
<li>Use correctly structured and semantically meaningful HTML</li>
</ul>
</section> 

